{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1148776-hurt-locker-grenade-questions","id":1148776,"title":"Hurt Locker grenade questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-11T01:22:55-07:00","id":1148776,"title":"Hurt Locker grenade questions","content":"I'm kind of confused as to how grenades work exactly. When you throw a grenade, you make a regular Throw Attack to see if you place it where you want it. What happens if you get 0 successes? Does that mean the grenade was a dud (didn't explode, didn't catch fire) or does it deviate somehow (are there even rules for deviation somewhere)?<br /> <br /> When the grenade goes off it does it's Damage to everyone in the Blast Radius. I'm guessing successes from the Throw Attack don't add to this damage, but instead you make a Force roll for everyone caught in the blast? If you get at least one success with the Force roll then you add the Damage again (effectively doubling the damage). Do successes from the Force roll add to damage as well? Why do molotovs have Force and Damage values? Don't they just set everyone caught in the Blast Radius on fire? Why do stun grenades have Force, but a Damage of +0. Why do thermite and white phosphorous grenade not have Force values? What kind of damage is the initial damage of Incendiaries? If I hit a vampire with a molotov, is the initial damage fire damage, or just some kind of generic damage? Do incendiaries still do aggravated/lethal/bashing damage depending on which Blast Radius band the victim is in?<br /> <br /> Was it ever official stated what the Ground Zero values are for grenades? I'm guessing it's meant to be half the listed Primary values?<br /> <br /> Have to say, the rules for explosives/grenades are a real mess. I think they could have used another look or two before being added to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 10-11-2017, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T10:49:00-07:00","id":1148863,"title":"","content":"It doesn't look like there is any new rules for throwing grenades in Hurt locker (or the God machine update, for that matter). The core rules simply say that if you don't get any successes on the grenade throw, then the GM decides were it lands. It also suggests that the location be worse for the character if they get a Dramatic Failure. There doesn't seem to be any kind of scatter chart, if that is what you are looking for, but it would be easy to homebrew (Ex roll one dice to determine direction it goes, one dice to determine how many meters it is off). As the saying goes, close counts with hand grenades.<br /> <br /> Extra successes on your throw roll don't lead to extra damage (though I am not sure if Defense is subtracted as usual, I could see that as case by case). It looks like the Force roll is essentially a normal attack, so its successes do count as damage. A 2 Damage frag grenade would do 2 damage to anyone caught in the blast, then roll three Force dice. If you get one success on this, it would deal the damage again, so you would deal 2+2+1. If you got two successes, it would be 2+2+2. Molotovs are treated as explosives, thus do damage as a normal explosive would in the same way thermite isn't really an explosive but is treated as one. I don't know why Stun grenades have a Force (as above it *would* deal damage for each success, but it states Stun grenades deal no damage in its blurb &gt;_&gt;). Probably supposed to be something for a different column. If you look at the thermite and WP grenades, you will notice that they don't have a reasonable initiative-they both have a Force of 4, but it looks off because they accidentally skipped a step (the table from the preview had a screwy format, probably leading to this error). The initial damage of incendiaries seems to be the same as the other explosives as written (Agg-Lethal-Bashing depending on your distance). I am not sure how you would rule the vampire thing, I'd probably consider it fire damage (since it isn't like it is sending chunks of metal at the vampire).<br /> <br /> I believe the official rules in Hurt Locker screwed up ground zero, I think half listed is what most people end up using.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the explosive rules are kinda a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}